a new protest staged by supporters of  shayat leader muqtada  this time in front of the supreme  judiciary council inside baghdad green  zone  they want the head of the supreme  judiciary council to resign and the  judiciary system to be reformed  we have been instructed by our leader to  protest here against the corrupt  judiciary system which is manipulated by  iran for years it has been collaborating  in impunity committed against the iraqi  people  we will be protesting until the  parliament is dissolved and inequitable  laws and constitutional articles are  amended  supporters of the shayat leader emerged  as the biggest party in parliament  following elections in october but they  were unable to form a government and  resign their seats two months ago  sadr's supporters have camped outside  the parliament for nearly a month  calling for it to be dissolved and early  elections held  but that's provoked the rivals raising  concerns of conflict  a counter protest is being held outside  the fences of the green zone  by supporters of the iranian-backed  parliamentary bloc known as the  coordination framework alliance or cfa  the latest escalation seems to be a  backlash against southern's movement  the supreme judiciary council has opened  an investigation into threats against  its staff by his supporters  and issued an arrest warrant against  approved other prominent politicians  the cfa has suspended all dialogues  other supporters until they end what  they call the occupation of the state  institutions  now the coordination framework has more  allies and more points for negotiation  they can embolden it to move on with  forming a government without members of  sardis party being part of it  earlier this month  southern rejected a national dialogue  initiative offered by caretaker prime  minister mustafa al-qademi  the supreme court has been handling  constitutional disputes between rival  parliamentary blocs  but southern side blames it for  derailing the formation of government  now with the country's judiciary system  at the heart of this conflict  many are questioning the integrity of  the iraq's political system
 

